# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in this file is a preference. Everything listed here is either
# third-party copyrighted material, machine-generated output, or local state.
#
# The corpus directories in particular MUST NEVER be committed: they hold
# academic papers that belong to their publishers and authors, plus the audio
# derived from them. This project ships the pipeline, never the corpus.
#
# NOTE ON SYNTAX: git does NOT support trailing comments. A line written as
# `pdfs/   # source PDFs` is a pattern containing spaces and a hash, and it
# matches nothing at all. Keep every comment on its own line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- the corpus: other people's papers, and everything derived from them ---
# downloaded or supplied source PDFs
pdfs/
# PDFs you supplied yourself
dropin/
# extracted full text of those PDFs
text/
# per-chunk narration WAVs
cache/
# concatenated per-paper audio and the M4B
out/
# uploaded attachments
files/
# upload staging
tmp/

# --- local state -----------------------------------------------------------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
# regenerated from workspace.sqlite on every mutation
papers.json
papers.json.part
papers.json.bak-*
# your machine's overrides, sourced by ./start.sh
local.env
# a systemd unit rendered for your machine by ./install-service.sh
*.service.local

# --- logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log

# --- python ----------------------------------------------------------------
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- node ------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
package-lock.json
npm-debug.log*

# --- editors / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
